    "body": "Addition by the maintainer, 2026-11-16:\n\n> \"outside machining like that should be entering from the inside and work up to the selected face or edge..\"\n\nThis replaces the \"Expected\" paragraph of the issue body. The body said that the tool starts outside the selected area. The maintainer's words are the requirement:\n\n- The tool enters from the inside of the area that the operation machines.\n- The passes then move toward the selected face or edge.\n- The selected face or edge is the limit where the passes stop.\n\nOpen point for the worker: record in the decision file which region \"the inside\" is for outside containment (the region between the stock side and the selected boundary), and where in that region the entry goes. Quote the maintainer's words there.\n\nDone means, in addition: the test shows that the first cut is at the entry in that region and that the last pass is at the selected face or edge.\n",
