    "body": "Findings before code. A decision is necessary.\n\n## Readings\n\nProbe: `fig8.step`, stock 5 mm past the part on each side, tool `EM-1000-4FL` (10 mm), 2D Adaptive, containment Outside.\n\n| Selected face | Extension | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| bottom face, Z 0 (the part stands on it) | 0 | `adaptive: the center area has no room for an entry` |\n| bottom face, Z 0 | 4 mm | generates; note `a piece of the area has no entry room - left uncut`; worst planned load 81.6 % of D |\n| top face, Z 20 | 0 or 4 mm | generates; the HSM plan is refused as a channel, and Offset rings cut it |\n\n## Cause\n\nThe entry search is not the cause. The cause is the area law (`crates/app/src/operation/boundary.rs`, step 5).\n\n- For a clearing kind, containment Outside grows the outline of the selection by one tool diameter, then removes the part (`containment_delta(ToolInside, Outside, r)` = 2r, `reach_past_edge`).\n- The generator keeps the full tool inside that area. Thus the tool center has a line of zero width, and no entry fits.\n- `crates/app/tests/shoulder_adaptive.rs` (`containment_outside_clears_past_the_edge_never_the_recess`) pins this refusal as correct behaviour today.\n\n## The decision\n\nThe requirement says: \"entering from the inside and work up to the selected face or edge\". This needs an area that is wider than the tool. Two options:\n\n1. **Area out to the stock.** With a stock, containment Outside on a clearing kind clears from the selected face out to the stock outline. The area goes one tool radius past the stock, so the outer passes run in air. The law already uses this rule for an open boundary. The entry is in the free area away from the face, and the last pass is at the face. Without a stock, the band of today stays, and the refusal names the Extension control.\n   - This changes the posted G-code of each clearing kind (Pocket, Adaptive and the others), not only 2D Adaptive.\n   - The pinned refusal in `shoulder_adaptive` becomes a generated toolpath.\n   - The work is probably `effort:max`.\n2. **Refusal by name only.** Keep the band of one tool. Replace the message with a refusal that names the control, for example: \"containment Outside leaves a band one tool wide around the selection - set an Extension (Boundary page) to give the tool room past the edge\". This is small and safe. It does not meet the addition of 2026-11-16 (enter inside, work up to the face).\n\nRecommendation: option 1, because it meets the requirement of the maintainer. Please select an option. The claim stays. No code is written until an option is selected.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
