    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T20:25:29Z",
    "body": "Addition by the maintainer in chat, 2026-11-16 (reported again as a bug):\n\n> \"2D Adaptive; Does not understand how to \"clear\" bulk material from outside of a model up to outer selected edge. Planning for bulk removal using an adaptive strategy.. Containment \"outside\" states \"Center area has no room for entry\" which makes no sense if its going to clear from outside in..\"\n\nReading of the orchestrator session (not the maintainer's words): this agrees with option 1 of the findings comment. Containment Outside on 2D Adaptive clears the bulk material between the stock outline and the selected outer edge. The band of one tool diameter does not meet this. Option 2 (a better refusal only) does not meet it.\n\nNotes:\n\n- The maintainer did not select an option by number. If the reading is wrong, he corrects it here.\n- The change is under the safety floor: it changes posted G-code of the clearing kinds. The verify check and the post gate stay unchanged.\n- Two claims are live on this issue (`vilts`, 2026-11-16T19:34Z; `mkinney`, 2026-11-16T20:20Z). The first claim holds the issue. The two claimants must agree who does the work.\n",
